{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill's description MUST state when to use it in terms of the user's task. It MAY name another bundled skill to use instead where an agent could confuse the two. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Site query.** `requirements.cli.skill_conventions/skills` selects the `<root>` of the five `assets/skills/*/SKILL.md` files: `habeas`, `habeas-requirements`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements` and `habeas-refactor`. A regex search for `^name:` and for a leading `---\\nname:` front matter finds exactly those five files and no others. The reference files under `references/` have no front matter and are not selected. The query therefore neither misses a skill nor selects anything out of scope. Its match snippet has front matter and its no_match snippet has none, which is enough for the `minus_metadata` condition.\n\n**Obligations.** The requirement has two: each description MUST state when to use the skill in terms of the user's task, and it MAY name another bundled skill to use instead where an agent could confuse the two. Each site upholds the first on its own, and the test also checks it for every skill. The MAY imposes nothing to check.\n\n**Test: `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skill_descriptions_say_when_to_use_them]`.**\n- For every skill in `SKILLS`, it parses the front matter and requires exactly one `name` equal to the skill's name. It requires exactly one non-empty `description` of at most 1024 characters, which equals `description(name)`.\n- For each of the five skills, it asserts that the description starts with a specific \"Use when/at/during …\" trigger phrase about the user's task.\n- It asserts that any `habeas-*` skill a description names is a bundled one.\n- It asserts that the pairs an agent could confuse each name the other skill to use instead: requirements to refactor and evidence, evidence to refactor, bootstrap to evidence, and refactor to requirements.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_are_five_skill_directories_each_home_to_its_topics]` asserts that `assets/skills` holds exactly the skills in `SKILLS`. So `SKILLS` cannot silently omit a bundled skill.\n\nNo adequacy gap found.",
